{"seq":4,"slug":"major-works","title":"查尔斯·达尔文·代表成就","stage":"DONE","category":"charles-darwin","categoryLabel":"查尔斯·达尔文","chapterCount":3,"docCount":6,"url":"/l-doc-books/c/people/charles-darwin/major-works","rating":{"composite":3.78,"verdict":"stable","groups":{"quality":3.6,"coverage":3.25,"positioning":3,"strategic":4},"weights":{"quality":0.3,"coverage":0.25,"positioning":0.2,"strategic":0.25},"profile":null},"hubDir":"/Users/wangyang.learnwy/learnwy/learnwy/l-doc-hub/hubs/famous-people/29_charles-darwin/4_major-works","introHtml":"<h1 id=\"查尔斯-达尔文的代表作\">查尔斯·达尔文的代表作</h1><p>达尔文远不止《物种起源》一部传世之作。本卷以&quot;书&quot;为单位，系统盘点他一生的代表性著作——从早年游记、地质专著，到两部改变世界的巨著，再到晚年精深的植物学与博物学专著——呈现一个作为持续写作者与博物学家的达尔文。</p>\n<h2 id=\"本卷-vs-兄弟卷-分工边界\">本卷 vs 兄弟卷：分工边界</h2><p>本卷只谈&quot;这些<strong>书本身</strong>&quot;：它们的版本沿革、论证结构、出版命运、文本贡献。与之相关但<strong>不在本卷展开</strong>的内容，请到对应兄弟卷：</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>想了解</th>\n<th>去哪一卷</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td>这些书背后<strong>理论</strong>的内涵（自然选择、性选择）</td>\n<td><a href=\"../core-contributions/\">代表贡献</a></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>达尔文的<strong>科学方法与思维风格</strong></td>\n<td><a href=\"../ideas-and-methods/\">思想与方法</a></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>写书时的<strong>生平经历</strong>（航行、晚年）</td>\n<td><a href=\"../life-and-times/\">生平与时代</a></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>这些书引发的<strong>社会·宗教震荡</strong></td>\n<td><a href=\"../influence-and-legacy/\">影响与遗产</a></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>针对这些书的<strong>科学质疑与伦理争议</strong></td>\n<td><a href=\"../controversies-and-appraisal/\">争议与评价</a></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>记忆口诀：本卷管&quot;书&quot;，贡献卷管&quot;理论&quot;，方法卷管&quot;怎么想&quot;，生平卷管&quot;何时何地写&quot;，影响/争议卷管&quot;写完之后发生了什么&quot;。</p>\n<h2 id=\"本卷三章\">本卷三章</h2><ol>\n<li><strong><a href=\"voyage-and-geology/\">航行与地质</a></strong>——<a href=\"voyage-and-geology/the-voyage-of-the-beagle-book\">《小猎犬号航行记》</a>与<a href=\"voyage-and-geology/geological-and-coral-reef-works\">地质学著作与珊瑚礁理论</a>，奠定其博物学家声誉、演练渐变论方法。</li>\n<li><strong><a href=\"the-great-books/\">两部巨著</a></strong>——<a href=\"the-great-books/on-the-origin-of-species\">《物种起源》</a>的论证结构与六版修订，以及把演化推及人类的<a href=\"the-great-books/the-descent-of-man-and-emotions\">《人类的由来》与情感表达</a>。</li>\n<li><strong><a href=\"botanical-and-final-works/\">植物学与最后的工作</a></strong>——<a href=\"botanical-and-final-works/orchids-climbing-and-insectivorous-plants\">兰花、攀缘植物与食虫植物</a>的实验演练，以及收官之作<a href=\"botanical-and-final-works/earthworms-and-final-work\">《蚯蚓与腐殖土》</a>。</li>\n</ol>\n<h2 id=\"推荐学习路径\">推荐学习路径</h2><ul>\n<li><strong>前置</strong>：无需专业背景；若对&quot;自然选择是什么&quot;完全陌生，建议先浏览 <a href=\"../core-contributions/natural-selection/\">代表贡献 · 自然选择</a>。</li>\n<li><strong>快速路径</strong>（只读一篇）：直接读 <a href=\"the-great-books/on-the-origin-of-species\">《物种起源》</a>。</li>\n<li><strong>完整路径</strong>（理解思想统一性）：按 航行游记 → 珊瑚礁地质 → 《物种起源》 → 《人类的由来》 → 植物学 → 蚯蚓 的顺序通读。这一顺序能看清贯穿全部著作的同一把钥匙——&quot;微小作用经漫长时间累积，造就宏大结构&quot;的渐变论世界观。</li>\n</ul>\n<p>通过梳理这些著作，本卷力图说明：达尔文的伟大不仅凝结于一部传世经典，更体现在他一生持续不辍、横跨地质·动物·人类·植物·土壤等众多领域、却由同一种思维方式贯穿始终的勤勉写作之中。</p>\n","chapters":[{"seq":1,"slug":"voyage-and-geology","title":"航行与地质著作","docCount":2,"url":"/l-doc-books/c/people/charles-darwin/major-works/voyage-and-geology","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"the-voyage-of-the-beagle-book","title":"《小猎犬号航行记》","url":"/l-doc-books/c/people/charles-darwin/major-works/voyage-and-geology/the-voyage-of-the-beagle-book"},{"seq":2,"slug":"geological-and-coral-reef-works","title":"地质学著作与珊瑚礁理论","url":"/l-doc-books/c/people/charles-darwin/major-works/voyage-and-geology/geological-and-coral-reef-works"}]},{"seq":2,"slug":"the-great-books","title":"奠基性巨著","docCount":2,"url":"/l-doc-books/c/people/charles-darwin/major-works/the-great-books","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"on-the-origin-of-species","title":"《物种起源》","url":"/l-doc-books/c/people/charles-darwin/major-works/the-great-books/on-the-origin-of-species"},{"seq":2,"slug":"the-descent-of-man-and-emotions","title":"《人类的由来》与情感表达","url":"/l-doc-books/c/people/charles-darwin/major-works/the-great-books/the-descent-of-man-and-emotions"}]},{"seq":3,"slug":"botanical-and-final-works","title":"植物学与晚期著作","docCount":2,"url":"/l-doc-books/c/people/charles-darwin/major-works/botanical-and-final-works","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"orchids-climbing-and-insectivorous-plants","title":"兰花、攀缘植物与食虫植物","url":"/l-doc-books/c/people/charles-darwin/major-works/botanical-and-final-works/orchids-climbing-and-insectivorous-plants"},{"seq":2,"slug":"earthworms-and-final-work","title":"《蚯蚓与腐殖土》与最后的工作","url":"/l-doc-books/c/people/charles-darwin/major-works/botanical-and-final-works/earthworms-and-final-work"}]}]}